.TH RIO-OPEN 1
.SH NAME
rio-open \- open a path in rio
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rio-open
[
.B -d
.I directory
]
.I path
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Rio-open
opens a directory in vdir or a text file in rio's built-in editor.
It is used as a plumber start action in the Halatha guest.
Relative paths are resolved against the working directory.
If /dev/wctl is absent, it attaches to the rio service named by $wsys.
Rio reads files in a separate process with a five-second I/O deadline and a
four-megabyte editor limit. UTF-8 is validated before the document is installed;
failed or partial reads do not become editable files.
.PP
Binary, non-UTF-8, and oversized files open a read-only hexadecimal and ASCII
preview in a separate terminal window. The preview reads at most 4096 bytes.
Missing files and read failures produce a visible error window.
The original file is not executed or changed by previewing it.
This fallback does not render image or document formats.
.PP
The
.B -d
option supplies the working directory for relative paths.
.SH SOURCE
.B /sys/src/cmd/rio-open.c
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR rio (1),
.IR rio (4),
.IR vdir (1),
.IR plumber (4)
